## Code Review: Duplicate Payment Callback Processing

### Root Cause Analysis

The `PaymentCallbackService.onCallback()` method has no idempotency protection. When a payment webhook is retried (common due to network issues, load balancer retries, etc.), the same provider transaction is processed multiple times, causing:

1. **Duplicate outbox entries** - `outboxRepository.insert()` is called for every callback
2. **Potential duplicate downstream processing** - Consumers of the outbox will see the same event multiple times

### The Fix

**File: `src/main/java/com/example/payment/PaymentCallbackService.java`**

Add an idempotency check before processing:

```java
public void onCallback(PaymentCallback payload) {
    Payment payment = paymentRepository.requireByOrderId(payload.getOrderId());

    // Idempotency: skip if this provider transaction already processed
    if (isAlreadyProcessed(payment, payload.getProviderTxnId())) {
        return;
    }

    payment.markPaid(payload.getProviderTxnId(), Instant.parse(payload.getPaidAt()));
    paymentRepository.save(payment);
    outboxRepository.insert("PAYMENT_PAID", payload.getOrderId(), payload.getProviderTxnId());
}

private boolean isAlreadyProcessed(Payment payment, String providerTxnId) {
    return "PAID".equals(payment.getStatus()) && providerTxnId.equals(payment.getProviderTxnId());
}
```

**File: `src/main/java/com/example/payment/Payment.java`**

Add missing getters for the idempotency check:

```java
public class Payment {
    private String orderId;
    private String providerTxnId;
    private String status;
    private Instant paidAt;

    public void markPaid(String providerTxnId, Instant paidAt) {
        this.providerTxnId = providerTxnId;
        this.paidAt = paidAt;
        this.status = "PAID";
    }

    // Add these getters
    public String getProviderTxnId() {
        return providerTxnId;
    }

    public String getStatus() {
        return status;
    }
}
```

